<p>Growing an Instagram account in Kenya, Nigeria, Ghana or anywhere on the continent comes with unique opportunities — and unique challenges. The audience is mobile-first, culturally nuanced and sceptical of brands that feel "foreign" or inauthentic. This playbook gives you the exact framework we use to grow African brand accounts consistently, without buying followers or using grey-hat tactics.</p>

<h2>Why Most African Brands Struggle on Instagram</h2>

<p>The common mistakes we see from brands across the continent:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Posting inconsistently — 3 posts this week, nothing for two weeks</li>
  <li>Only posting product photos with zero storytelling</li>
  <li>Using overly formal, corporate language that does not connect</li>
  <li>Ignoring comments and DMs</li>
  <li>Copying Western content formats that do not resonate locally</li>
  <li>Focusing on follower count instead of engagement and sales</li>
</ul>

<blockquote>1,000 engaged followers who buy from you are worth more than 50,000 ghost followers who ignore every post. Build the right audience first.</blockquote>

