<h2>The 4-Pillar Content Framework</h2>

<p>Every post you create should fit into one of these four categories. A healthy account rotates through all four weekly:</p>

<h3>Pillar 1: Educate (30% of content)</h3>
<p>Share useful, actionable tips related to your industry. This builds authority and gets saved (saves are the highest-value engagement signal on Instagram).</p>
<p>Examples: "3 things to check before hiring a plumber in Nairobi" / "How to know if your accountant is cheating you" / "5 signs your child needs glasses"</p>

<h3>Pillar 2: Entertain (25% of content)</h3>
<p>Relatable content, memes, behind-the-scenes videos, day-in-the-life Reels. Content that makes people feel something — laughter, nostalgia, pride. This drives shares and reach.</p>
<p>Examples: A funny Reel of what Monday mornings look like at your office / A "before and after" transformation video / Staff introduction posts with personality</p>

<h3>Pillar 3: Inspire (20% of content)</h3>
<p>Success stories, client results, brand mission content. This builds emotional connection and trust. For African audiences, content that celebrates local success and ambition performs especially well.</p>
<p>Examples: A client testimonial told as a mini story / "We started this business from a bedsitter in Nairobi" origin story / Milestone celebration posts</p>

<h3>Pillar 4: Convert (25% of content)</h3>
<p>Direct offers, product showcases, service promotions, calls to action. Do not be shy about selling — but always lead with value before the ask.</p>
<p>Examples: "We have 3 slots left for June — book your free strategy session" / Product feature posts with pricing / Limited-time offers</p>

<h2>Reels: The Fastest Path to Reach</h2>

<p>Instagram's algorithm heavily favours Reels over static posts. If you are not posting at least 3 Reels per week, you are limiting your reach significantly. Here is our Reels formula:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Hook in the first 2 seconds</strong>: Start with a bold statement, question or surprising visual. "This Nairobi restaurant made Sh4M in one month from Instagram."</li>
  <li><strong>Keep it under 30 seconds</strong>: Shorter Reels get replayed more, which signals the algorithm to push them wider.</li>
  <li><strong>Use trending audio</strong>: Pair your content with trending songs or sounds for extra algorithmic boost.</li>
  <li><strong>Add on-screen text</strong>: Many users watch with sound off. Captions are essential.</li>
  <li><strong>Strong CTA at the end</strong>: "Follow for more" / "Save this for later" / "Comment your city below"</li>
</ul>

